Looking at ioctl.c, there are several possible
compiler defines that could push the search for
termio.h down to /usr/include/sys/termio.h , though
they'd probably all be erroneous if enabled.  Try
putting a copy of the existing /usr/include/termio.h
down there (it should defend itself against being
doubly included) and see if that helps.

Though you are compiling in a "Unix-like"
environment, it may be that choosing the "Unix"
compilation style isn't the appropriate option, but
putting a copy of termio.h where it might be
encountered is at least a good first attempt at a
fix. If nothing else, you might get past the current
stopping point just to see a new, different one that
gives more information about the source of the
difficulty.

Is this a new cygwin installation, or a different
piece of hardware (or updated MS_Win release) than
where you built 3.4.0? The usual reason for
following any of those #ifdef paths would be a
changed external environment.

